@@ -304,3 +304,28 @@ not an imported emulator source file. No game-generated source is included.
 The pinned user-game generation has no calls to these named helpers; the tests
 therefore exercise synthetic operands explicitly. Compilation/native results
 do not establish target execution; the consolidated Switch run remains required.
+
+
+## Switch compiled VU strict policy (M02, 2026-11-09)
+
+[gta-recomp] `tools/vu1_recomp.py` generated registration selects the full
+bookkeeping/exact-range variant when `__SWITCH__` or
+`PS2X_VU1_COMPILED_PRECISE` is defined. Desktop defaults remain unchanged.
+The runtime still uses its fast interpreter mode, so compiled selection remains
+eligible; this does not select the cycle-exact interpreter or bypass shape/code
+identity checks.
+
+The public synthetic differential test exposed two differences in the old
+throughput `_t` variant: MADD with FLT_MAX * 2 and ACC=-1 produced 0x7f7ffffe
+while the interpreter's exact-range rule clamps to 0x7f7fffff; an arithmetic
+program took 10 cycles compiled versus 15 in the same fast interpreter. The
+throughput emission deliberately omits VF/VI/ACC readiness and uses plain
+MADD/MSUB. Selecting the existing full variant preserves all MADD/MSUB forms
+(including ACC destinations) and their numeric range checks, as well as the
+existing stall/ready/settle model. No numerical test input or cycle comparison
+is relaxed. This is a correctness baseline; no target performance is claimed.
+
+Generated private game VU code must be regenerated after this change so its
+registration contains the policy. Public fixture generation records both the
+pristine generator pin/hash and this effective overlaid generator identity.
+The root port retains the failing and passing synthetic traces.
